{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1548682-rage-across-texas-my-campaign-s-ideas","id":1548682,"title":"Rage Across Texas (my campaign's ideas)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-02-21T11:35:23-08:00","id":1548682,"title":"Rage Across Texas (my campaign's ideas)","content":"Hello, everyone.<br /> <br /> Just wanted to share with you some of my ideas for a W20 campaign that I've been working on lately. But first, some background info: I run a lot of different games in the 90s and 2000s, and W:tA was one of them. I've had three long campaigns (the first one was set in Great Britain, the second one was a Wyld West, where the players' pack was successful in bringing the Croatan back to life, and the last one was set in NYC).<br /> <br /> I've recently purchased the Core Book for the 20th Anniversary Edition, plus some other books, and reading them got my creative juices flowing again, to the point I'm feeling inspired to start another campaign (or chronicle, as you prefer) after a long time, and it will take place in the same timeline of the previous three (so that means that the Croatan do exist in my canon. Also, my personal canon differs a lot (and I mean a lot!) lore-wise from &quot;official&quot; canon.<br /> <br /> For instance, the <b>White Howlers</b> are still around (long story, but I can share with anyone who's interested). And the <b>Red Talons</b> are not the genocidal maniacs of the canon; instead, they're the Wyld tribe in pretty much the same way the GW are the Weaver tribe, and thus have a much healthier relationship with the rest of the Garou Nation. They're still all-lupus, though.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I've decided on setting this campaign in Texas (I'm not American, but I've visited the state quite a few times and I love it). And in case someone is curious, my home country has no native wolf population, that's why I chose the US. Also, in this setting, due to the actions of Garou kinfolk the Texas wolf (<i>Canis lupus monstrabilis</i>) is still around and far from extinct.<br /> <br /> Anyway, here are some of the ideas I had for the Texan caerns (I've posted this on White Wolf's sub-Reddit, so it's possible some of you may already have read it).<br /> <br /> <b>Sept of the Ancient Wisdom</b><br /> Located at Big Bend Nacional Park, level 5 Memory Caern.<br /> Totem: the Rattlesnake<br /> Tribal structure: Uktena and Croatan. Wendigo, Silent Striders, and Red Talons are welcome.<br /> <br /> <b>Sept of the Cloudy Mountains</b><br /> Located at the Guadalupe Mountains, level 4 Courage Caern.<br /> Totem: the Puma<br /> Tribal structure: Uktena, with Silent Striders and Red Talons. Pumonca are welcome.<br /> <br /> <b>Sept of the Hard Wood</b><br /> Located at the Palo Duro Canyon, level 4 Stamina Caern.<br /> Totem: the Bison<br /> Tribal structure: Uktena, with CoG and Fianna<br /> <br /> <b>Sept of the Misty Lake</b><br /> Located at Caddo Lake, level 3 Gnosis Caern.<br /> Totem: the Fog<br /> Tribal structure: Uktena, Bone Gnawers, and CoG<br /> <br /> <b>Sept of the Enchanted Rock</b><br /> Located at Enchanted Rock, Hill Country, level 3 Strength Caern.<br /> Totem: Granite<br /> Tribal structure: Get of Fenris<br /> <br /> <b>Sept of the Big River Valley</b><br /> Located at the Rio Grande Valley, southeastern TX, level 3 War Caern.<br /> Totem: Tobadzistsini<br /> Tribal structure: Uktena, with Black Furies, Fianna and Red Talons<br /> <br /> <i>Note: this is the most recent Caern opened in Texas, its main purpose is to fight a drug cartel controlled by the Black Spiral Dancers and their kinfolk that has been operating in the region for a while</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>Sept of the Clear Mountains</b><br /> Located at Davis Mountains, level 3 leadership Caern.<br /> Totem: Falcon (maybe Bald Eagle)<br /> Tribal structure: Silver Fangs, with Get of Fenris and Fianna<br /> <br /> <b>Sept of H-Town</b><br /> Located in Houston, level 3 (maybe level 2) Urban Caern;<br /> Totem: the Yellow-Crowned Night Heron<br /> Tribal structure: Glass Walkers and Shadow Lords<br /> <br /> <b>Sept of the Lone Star</b><br /> Located in the Great Trinity Forest, Dallas, level 3 Fellowship Caern.<br /> Totem: the Flying Red Horse<br /> Tribal structure: maintained by the Glass Walkers, but Black Furies, Bone Gnawers, Children of Gaia, Fianna, Get of Fenris, and Silent Striders are present. Since it is a fellowship caern, other tribes and Fera are welcome.<br /> <br /> <b>Sept of the Healing Waters</b><br /> Located in the Fort Worth Nature Center &amp; Refuge, level 3 (maybe 2) Caern, haven't decided on type yet, either Healing or Elemental (Water).<br /> Totem: Akokisa, the <i>incarna</i> of Trinity River.<br /> Tribal structure: CoG and Uktena<br /> <br /> <i>Note: I'm not sure whether the Dallas-Fort Worth Metroplex will have two Caerns, as above, or if it's batter to make a single, large Caern with two separate centers (one in the forest and the other one in the Nature Center) and two different totems.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28735,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28735-greywolf76","user":"Greywolf76","date":". 03-19-2025, 11:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28735-greywolf76","name":"Greywolf76","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28735_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-21T13:08:37-08:00","id":1548687,"title":"","content":"So wait, if the Howlers are still about then where do Our Heroes get their steady supply of Evil Werewolves to maul?<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, Texas sounds like a fine place for some CAPTAIN PLANET WITH MURDERS action: being an essentially larger-than-life place, it\u2019s easy to imagine it suiting the Old World of Darkness\u2019 most Blood &amp; Thunder game line.<br /> <br /> Well, most Thunder and Lightning game line - VAMPIRE would probably dispatch a colony of rabid bats to my immediate vicinity if I pretended any other game line was more \u2018Blood\u2019.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28339,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","user":"Atticus Cleanclaw","date":". 02-21-2025, 04:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-23T14:56:44-08:00","id":1548739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1548682-rage-across-texas-my-campaign-s-ideas?p=1548687#post1548687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So wait, if the Howlers are still about then where do Our Heroes get their steady supply of Evil Werewolves to maul?</div> </div> </div> </div>My canon is not so different. BSD are still corrupted, Wyrm-worshiping Garou, but the first ones were not created from a single tribe. They were breeding in secret for centuries before revealing themselves when they invaded Caledonia (around the same time the Howlers fell in official canon).<br /> <br /> The other difference is that in my canon other Garou answered the White Howlers call for help during this invasion. First the Fianna, them the get of Fenris, Silver Fangs, and CoG. They are still around but are one of the smallest tribes, alongside the Stargazers. They still got a hold in Scotland, which they share with the Fianna, and also are common in the Maritime Provinces of Canada, particularly Nova Scotia.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28735-greywolf76","name":"Greywolf76","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28735_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-25T11:19:40-08:00","id":1548766,"title":"","content":"Fair enough - individuals danced the Black Spiral long before the Howlers went to Hell - though for my money losing that particular Epic Tragedy - costs the setting something (Of only a cautionary tale of what happens when a Tribe places Wisdom a distant third behind Glory &amp; Honour).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-18T06:05:01-07:00","id":1549405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1548682-rage-across-texas-my-campaign-s-ideas?p=1548766#post1548766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair enough - individuals danced the Black Spiral long before the Howlers went to Hell - though for my money losing that particular Epic Tragedy - costs the setting something (Of only a cautionary tale of what happens when a Tribe places Wisdom a distant third behind Glory &amp; Honour).</div> </div> </div> </div>You got a very strong point, Atticus. Thanks.<br /> <br /> I'm still in the early stages of rewriting the setting (mostly changing themes, mood, and a few things I personally think don't work anymore for me as a game master), so suggestions and ideas are always welcome.<br /> <br /> But you're right, having an entire tribe changing sides is a powerful setting element that also serves a cautionary tale to the Garou: &quot;Remember the lost tribe, cub. This is what happens when you let hubris and cruelty dictate your actions&quot;.<br /> <br /> Since I want to keep the White Howlers around, I might tie the origins of the BSD to another tribe - an isolationist, cruel, arrogant, and self-centered tribe that either tried to invade Malfeas and fell prey to their own hubris, or just changed sides because they had already succumbed to their wrath and cruelty, and thought the Garou Nation were a bunch of wussies.<br /> <br /> Might even put them in the Arctic and call them &quot;Galestalkers&quot;, or just keep referring to them as the &quot;lost tribe&quot;, since their infamy made their name lost in the mists of time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28735-greywolf76","name":"Greywolf76","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28735_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-18T17:58:26-07:00","id":1549427,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28735-greywolf76\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar28735_1.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28735\" data-vbnamecard=\"28735\">Greywolf76</a>, thank you most kindly for your own courteous replies - my own suggestion would be to run with \u2018The Lost\u2019 or \u2018The Lost Tribe\u2019, since the very name<br /> of that tribe having become taboo allows a sense of the sheer scope of the betrayal, while also allowing you the option to come up with an actual name at your leisure (Also to avoid confusion with Younger Brother by the use of \u2018Galestalkers\u2019).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-18T18:09:09-07:00","id":1549428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1548682-rage-across-texas-my-campaign-s-ideas?p=1549427#post1549427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28735-greywolf76\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar28735_1.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28735\" data-vbnamecard=\"28735\">Greywolf76</a>, thank you most kindly for your own courteous replies - my own suggestion would be to run with \u2018The Lost\u2019 or \u2018The Lost Tribe\u2019, since the very name<br /> of that tribe having become taboo allows a sense of the sheer scope of the betrayal, while also allowing you the option to come up with an actual name at your leisure (Also to avoid confusion with Younger Brother by the use of \u2018Galestalkers\u2019).</div> </div> </div> </div>What do The Lost call eachother? How does this Title unify them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/448972/Hearthbound-Tribe-Supplement?affiliate_id=4046720\" target=\"_blank\">Hearthbound</a> and Project Director for <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/songoftrillium/729204622290550784/likes-dont-increase-visibility-to-others-please\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Essentials</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27167-mundusartis","name":"mundusartis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27167_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-18T18:30:31-07:00","id":1549432,"title":"","content":"Presumably they call themselves \u2018The Winning Side\u2019.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}